        "procedure": "Compound 2 was obtained by CuI-catalyzed azide–alkyne cycloaddition of 1 with methoxypoly(ethylene glycol) alkyne (PEG, 2000 g mol−1) in toluene/acetonitrile. FTIR and 1H NMR show loss of the azide (~2117 cm−1) and alkyne (~3250 cm−1; alkyne proton at 2.45 ppm) signals. EDS and ICP-OES give Eu/Ti ≈ 8/10, and ICP-OES indicates an average of about three PEG chains per cluster and a molecular weight of approximately 14000 g mol−1. Numerical reagent amounts are not given in the main text (referred to Supporting Information, Synthesis and Table S2), and no SI file was supplied.",
